{"_v":1,"id":"king-hedley-ii-2001","cat":"broadway","bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":2,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://theater.nytimes.com/mem/theater/treview.html?res=9401E5DF1738F931A35756C0A9679C8B63","d":"2001-05-02","q":"Voices go hurtling to heaven in August Wilson’s 'King Hedley II,' gut-deep cries of confusion that keep pushing toward some elusive ecstasy of understanding."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2001/legit/news/king-hedley-ii-2-1200468606/","d":"2001-05-01","q":"It's telling that the audience hears pop songs by Michael Jackson and the Commodores as it is taking its seats, but the music in the play is strictly retro: jazzy blues and even a waltz."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/page/world/KingHedley.html","d":"2001-05-02","q":"King Hedley II feels like a work with the best of intentions that keeps getting trod on at the wrong time."}],"au":{"score":75,"designation":"Shrugging","sources":{"mz":{"s":75,"c":2,"sr":3.8}}},"tn":[{"yr":55,"cat":"Best Featured Actress in a Play","n":"Viola Davis","w":true},{"yr":55,"cat":"Best Play","n":null},{"yr":55,"cat":"Best Actor in a Play","n":"Brian Stokes Mitchell"},{"yr":55,"cat":"Best Actress in a Play","n":"Leslie Uggams"},{"yr":55,"cat":"Best Featured Actor in a Play","n":"Charles Brown"},{"yr":55,"cat":"Best Direction of a Play","n":"Marion McClinton"}],"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":2479599,"p":96,"a":68803}},"pd":"2001-04-10","ca":[{"n":"Brian Stokes Mitchell","r":"King"},{"n":"Leslie Uggams","r":"Ruby"},{"n":"Charles Brown","r":"Elmore"},{"n":"Viola Davis","r":"Tonya"},{"n":"Stephen McKinley Henderson","r":"Stool Pigeon"},{"n":"Monté Russell","r":"Mister"}]}